# [[.Name]]

[[.Title]]: [[.Summary]]. Generated by kickhub from `[[.Template]]` v[[.Version]], target **[[.Target]]**.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `app/model.py` | Loads the artifact and predicts. The only file to change for your own model. |
| `app/main.py` | FastAPI routes: `GET /healthz`, `POST /predict`, with input validation |
| `model.json` | Example model artifact (three weights and a bias) |
| `tests/` | API tests, including rejected inputs |
[[ if eq .Target "local" -]]
| `docker-compose.yml` | The service in a container on port 8080 |
[[- else -]]
| `infra/` | Registry, runtime identity and the serving service |
[[- end ]]
| `.kickhub.yaml` | Records the template, version and parameters used |

## Run it

```sh
make test
make run       # http://localhost:8080/docs for the interactive API
```
[[ if eq .Target "local" ]]
```sh
make up && make smoke
make down
```
[[ else if eq .Target "aws" ]]
```sh
make infra-apply                      # registry and roles
aws ecr get-login-password --region [[.P.aws_region]] | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin "$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw ecr_repository_url | cut -d/ -f1)"
make image REPO="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw ecr_repository_url)"
make infra-apply IMAGE_URI="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw ecr_repository_url):$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)"
terraform -chdir=infra output service_url
```
[[ else ]]
```sh
make infra-apply                      # registry and service account
gcloud auth configure-docker [[.P.gcp_region]]-docker.pkg.dev
make image REPO="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw image_repository)"
make infra-apply IMAGE_URI="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw image_repository):$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)"
terraform -chdir=infra output service_url
```
[[ end ]]
## Serving your own model

1. Replace `model.json` with your artifact and load it in `Model.load`.
2. Add its library to `requirements.txt`.
3. Keep `model_version` in the response: it is what lets you tell which model answered when two versions are live.

The API has no authentication. Put it behind your gateway before exposing it.
